# Solidity Contract Development

## ABI Regeneration Policy (No Manual ABI Edits)

If any contract ABI can change (function/event/error/signature changes), regenerate ABIs with commands. Do not manually edit:

- individual ABI files under `apps/web/src/abi/` (`BasketVault.ts`, `OracleAdapter.ts`, etc.) or the barrel `contracts.ts`
- files under `apps/envio/abis/`

Run:

```bash
PATH="/Users/reuben/.foundry/bin:$PATH" forge build --root /Users/reuben/Desktop/minestarters/code/snx-prototype
node scripts/extract-abis.js
for c in BasketFactory BasketVault BasketShareToken VaultAccounting OracleAdapter StateRelay; do jq '.abi' "out/$c.sol/$c.json" > "apps/envio/abis/$c.json"; done
```

`ERC20.json` in `apps/envio/abis/` is a stable external ABI and is not regenerated from local `out/`.

## Local Redeploy Rule (When Docker Compose Is Running)

When contract code changes and the local Docker Anvil is running (`npm run local:up`), redeploy contracts instead of leaving stale deployments.

Use:

```bash
npm run redeploy:local
```

This deploys contracts to Docker Anvil and updates `apps/web/src/config/local-deployment.json`. The Next.js dev server (started with `npm run local:dev`) picks up new addresses via HMR.

If the Envio indexer is running (`npm run --prefix apps/envio dev:local`), restart it after contract redeploys so it picks up the new addresses from `config.local.generated.yaml`.
